{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And Moshe and Aharon did all these wonders.</b> These are the ten plagues that he has arranged until now, and the mnemonic for them is דצ״ך עד״ש באח״ב, and this is the order set out in the Torah. And they were divided into four parts corresponding to the four elements: blood and frogs from the water. And it would have been fitting for the earth to be smitten first, for it is the lowest element, but since all the earth drinks from the Nile, therefore he began by smiting the waters — for when it is smitten, all the elements are smitten along with it; therefore the waters were smitten and their particular creatures, which are the fish, died. Lice and wild beasts from the dust, which is stronger than water — as it is written, ״כל עפר הארץ היה כנים״, and it is written, ״ותשחת הארץ״ etc. And since he hardened his heart and would not send them forth, He brought upon him plagues from the heavens upon their bodies: from the element of air — pestilence upon the bodies of the beasts; and from the element of fire — boils upon the bodies of man; and from the element of air again — hail and locusts upon the vegetation of the ground. And still they did not heed this, and He brought upon them a plague from the air, which is darkness, and the destruction of the breath of the spirit of life that was in the firstborn. And as for what is written, ״עשו את כל המופתים״ — Moshe and Aharon did not perform any act in the plague of wild beasts, nor in the plague of pestilence, nor in the plague of the firstborn; rather, it speaks of the majority. And note: in seven plagues it is said of them ״נטית היד״ (you shall stretch out your hand), apart from these three, and the verse will explain to you that after ten plagues had been completed upon them, still the Holy One, blessed be He, strengthened his heart, to fulfill what was said to him at the outset, ״ואני אקשה את לבו״; and so we find at the Sea, where it is written there, ״ויחזק ה׳ את לב פרעה מלך מצרים וירדוף אחרי בני ישראל״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Mnemonic דצ״ך עד״ש באח״ב stands for דם צפרדע כנים / ערוב דבר שחין / ברד ארבה חושך בכורות. Citation 'ותשחת הארץ' alludes to Genesis 6:11. The phrase 'האחרון' for earth is rendered 'lowest' following the medieval element-order convention."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:57.536848776Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}